      summary: String.raw`A symplectic form is a closed, non-degenerate 2-form; the cotangent bundle of any manifold carries a canonical one, and Darboux’s theorem says all symplectic manifolds look alike locally. Functions generate Hamiltonian flows that preserve the form, hence volume, which is the geometric content of Hamiltonian mechanics. Symmetries give conserved quantities, and rigidity phenomena such as non-squeezing show symplectic maps are far more constrained than volume-preserving ones.`,
